FYI for everyone:

I was using the "JSONlite" package in my app. Here's some technobabble from a subsequently deleted Github issue <https://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:CxFTcHiJtAQJ:https://github.com/rstudio/shinyapps/issues/120+&cd=1&hl=en&ct=clnk&gl=us> about how JSONlite sometimes needs HTTR, and sometimes doesn't (?!?). Due to this behavior, explicitly calling library(httr) is apparently necessary. This removed my problem.

Soo... hooray for hidden dependency bombs?

