Hi Jake,
Unfortunately shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> doesn't have a mechanism for scheduling execution of work.  It is one of those ideas we have been considering but hadn't seen enough demand for. You are the second person to bring it up in the past 24 hours so perhaps the idea is gaining more momentum now.  Right now, your best bet would like be to run the code on a machine that you can schedule the work on (example crontab) and push the resulting data to a place that is accessible from shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> (dropbox, S3, or a database like Redshift).  Once we add support for persistent storage, and scheduling it will be a much simpler process to do what you want to do.

-Tareef

